  "intentional_matching_changes": [
    "Replace generic-header exfiltration conviction with explicit declared theft channel plus file-read and HTTP-send API evidence.",
    "Detect exported steal/lock task interface without requiring a particular domain, payload filename or export spelling.",
    "Consolidate machine/device identity headers in their HTTP header home; preserve informative neutral header observations.",
    "Require MZ and PE signature comparison context around the +0x3c read; an arbitrary struct field is insufficient.",
    "Replace ambiguous digest word with the existing actual digest-method observation in its sole consumer.",
    "Canonical Start-Process grouping combines parser-confirmed calls and embedded FilePath command text; underlying observations remain separate.",
    "Correct string-count description: exclusions cover recognized software contexts, not every compiler.",
    "Ancestor selectors now exclude launch options from process creation and neutral headers from exfiltration. Exact consumers were rewritten. Direct hidden-option any-consumers explicitly retain the moved option umbrella."
  ],
  "placement_checks": [
    "Claim-first pass: distinguish neutral protocol fields and options, file properties, API lifecycle operations, and attacker task/exfil objectives.",
    "Resource-first pass: headers -> HTTP/header/custom; flags -> process/argument/option; context -> crypto/provider; hash init -> crypto/hash/digest; string counts -> file/profile/string-population; PE checks -> data/parse/portable-executable; ShellExecute -> process/create/shellexec; output configuration -> process/fd/stdio; actual reads/writes -> process/io/stream.",
    "New intent findings use file source rather than asserting browser provenance from generic names; task handler finding does not assert HTTP task polling."
